<title>CANADA: Canada approves Arctic diamond mine.</title>
<headline>Canada approves Arctic diamond mine.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada on Friday gave final approval for an Arctic diamond mine proposed by Australian giant Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd and Dia Met Minerals Ltd of Canada.</p>
<p>Northern Development Minister Ron Irwin gave the final go-ahead for the C$860 million (S647 million) project during an official ceremony in Yellowknife, the capital of the Northwest Territories, the federal government said in a statement.</p>
</text>
